1. WHAT YOU MAY DO

The Software is free. Offset Security grants you a licence, at no charge, to:

  a. install and run the Software on as many computers as you like, inside
     your own organisation;
  b. use it for any purpose, commercial or otherwise, including work you are
     paid for;
  c. let as many of your own people use it as you like;
  d. keep and use everything you put into it — your data is yours; and
  e. pass on the Software to others, provided you pass it on complete,
     unmodified, at no charge, and with this agreement included.

This licence is non-exclusive and can be ended as set out in section 7.


2. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

You may not:

  a. modify, adapt or translate the Software, or create anything derived
     from it;
  b. reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble the compiled Software,
     except where law says you may despite this term;
  c. remove, alter, hide or obscure the Offset Security name, logo, product
     names, copyright notices or the notices in section 5 — anywhere they
     appear, including on screen and in exported reports;
  d. re-brand or white-label the Software, or present it as your own product
     or as anyone else's;
  e. sell, rent, lease, sublicense or charge for the Software;
  f. run it as a service for people outside your own organisation, whether
     paid or free;
  g. use the Offset Security name, logos or product names to promote anything,
     or in a way that suggests Offset Security endorses you; or
  h. use it to break the law.

For the avoidance of doubt: the Software includes a feature for adding your
own organisation's logo to reports you export. Using that feature is expressly
permitted and is not a breach of 2(c) or 2(d). It adds your logo to your
documents; it does not remove ours from the product.


