4. WHO OWNS WHAT

Offset Security owns the Software and everything in it, and keeps that
ownership. This agreement licenses the Software to you; it does not sell it to
you. Anything not expressly granted here is reserved.

You own your data. The Software stores everything on the systems you run it
on. It sends nothing to Offset Security and contains no telemetry or usage
tracking. It never checks for updates by itself: only when an administrator
presses the button in Settings does it contact Offset Security's release page,
to see whether a newer version exists. Nothing else leaves your machines unless
you send it yourself.


